    "body": "## End-to-end work summary\nOn a laptop whose person chose a server (a Mac mini) with \"Make ... my home\", the background updater downloads updates, but the page the window shows gets no update bridge. Settings → This app shows an inert \"Check for updates\", the sidebar says \"Up to date\", and there is no \"Restart to update\". Main now treats the page of the server chosen as home, while the window shows it, like My Cloud's page for the update channels (`update:offered`, check, install, state, seen). The page reads real state, so the sidebar line, banner and Updates row follow it. The change is `ownHomePage` in `updaterPageAllowed` (`electron/main.mjs`, on an existing source line, so the size limit holds) and `ownHome.target()` (`electron/own-home-main.mjs`), the chosen server's address.\n\n## Subagent delegation\nNone. Subagents were not available in this session.\n\n## Technical decisions\n- The gate is: the main frame's origin equals the active environment's origin equals `ownHome.target()`. The page can only ask to check, read state or install. Install still needs a user click in preload. It never picks a URL or file.\n- The gate uses the chosen server, not `ownHome.origin()`. `origin()` is set only after the move finished. On the laptop the choice exists but the move has not started, so `origin()` would be null and the fix would not have applied.\n- `desktopRemoteAccess || cloudSignInRestored` in `updaterPageOffered` is unchanged. It still keeps every other server's page from the updater.\n- The renderer needs no change. The page already reads updater state (`useAppSubLine`, `UpdateBanner`, `UpdatesRow`). Once main offers the bridge they show the real state. The page comes from the server's build, so a renderer-only fix would not reach the laptop.\n\n## Deviations from plan\nThe brief named `desktopRemoteAccess` (remote client mode) as the cause. The evidence does not support it, so this PR does not touch that rule. In remote client mode the page is the local origin, which already gets the full bridge, and a new test pins that. The laptop shows a different mode (below).\n\n## Completion evidence\nEvidence chain, with rival hypotheses eliminated:\n1. **Background check skipped?** No. `startUpdater` (`electron/updater.mjs`, last lines) schedules a first check after 15 s and then hourly, with no remote or home condition. The laptop's `updater.log` shows `Checking for update`, a full download of 0.1.169-mf.2 into `~/Library/Caches/openmausbot-updater/pending`, and `nativeUpdater.update-downloaded`.\n2. **Feed stale?** No. `https://gamestudio.mobigame.vn/openmausbot-desktop/latest-mac.yml` serves `version: 0.1.169-mf.2`, and the log shows that download.\n3. **Which mode is the laptop in?** Not remote client. `server.log` shows its own local server (`server ready ... port=8799`). `environments.json` has activeId = the Mac mini (`kind: remote`, no `home`/`cloud`/`team` flag). `own-home-choice.json` holds the Mac mini as chosen home, and `own-home.json` holds no move journal. So `home.away()` is false and `ownHome.origin()` is null.\n4. **Page offered the updater?** No. `updaterPageAllowed` (`electron/main.mjs:2558` before the fix) accepted only `cloudPageAsking` (this computer, My Cloud) or `ownCloudPage`, and `homeWindow.homePage` follows My Cloud only. After the sign-in restore, `updaterPageOffered` returned false (`main.mjs:2560-2561`), so `preload.cjs:123` gave the page no `updater` key. `AppPages.tsx:45-55` then rendered the inert row.\n5. **State not forwarded?** Same cause. `setState` in `updater.mjs` sends `update:state` only to a page that `pageAllowed` accepts, and the `update:get-state`, check and install handlers throw for any other page.\n6. **Red then green.** `electron/updater.test.mjs` \"the server the person made their home gets the update bridge and its channels while the window shows it, and no other server does\" fails against `origin/main`'s `main.mjs` (1 failed, 12 passed) and passes with the fix (13 passed). It covers offered, the bridge keys, check, install, state, seen, a different active server, a frame of another origin, and no choice. \"a laptop connected to another computer as its client keeps the update bridge on its own page\" covers remote client mode. `electron/own-home-main.node-test.mjs` covers `target()`: set before the move finishes, null without a choice.\n7. **Fresh runs on the final tree:** `pnpm test:electron`: 2172 pass, 0 fail. `vitest` for `updater.test.mjs`, `SettingsModal.updates.test.ts` and `file-size-ratchet.test.ts`: 17 pass. `oxlint --deny-warnings .`: exit 0. `pnpm typecheck` (tsc -b, server, phone-protocol): exit 0.\n8. **Frontend verification:** no renderer file changed. The Updates row test (`SettingsModal.updates.test.ts`) pins that the check is offered on a page with no `home` and no `remoteClient`. I did not run a browser, because the page comes from the Mac mini's build and the gate is in main.\n\n## Checklist\n- [x] Root cause proven with logs, state files and code lines\n- [x] Rival hypotheses eliminated\n- [x] Test fails before the fix and passes after\n- [x] Lint, typecheck, electron tests, size ratchet\n- [ ] Manual check on the laptop after installing the fixed build\n\n## Human actions required\nThe gate lives in the installed app, so the app now on the laptop cannot get it by itself. Install the first build with this fix by hand. After that, Settings → This app and the sidebar follow the real update state while the window shows the Mac mini. An update the background updater already downloaded then shows \"Restart to update\".\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
